items.description:
One op (fields per kind; ? = optional). A ref is a node id, @key (a node created earlier in this call) or @copyKey/<original id> (that node inside a copy made earlier in this call); parent also takes "root". key names the new node; index = position among siblings (default: append); node = one .kimo node body {type, name?, …fields}, never with children (each child is its own insert with parent @key), e.g. {"type":"text","content":"Hello","style":{"size":16}} (kimo_read_docs path=schema); set = {field: value} (shallow; null removes the field).
insert {key?, parent, at?, index?, node}
update {id, set?, unset?:[]}
replace {id, node}
move {id, parent, at?, index?}
delete {id}
copy {id, key?, parent, at?, index?, set?}
set_variables {set?:[{name, variable}], unset?:[]}
set_theme_axes {set?:[{axis, values:[]}], unset?:[]}
instantiate {of, key?, parent, at?, index?, x?, y?, name?}
make_component {ids:[], key?, name?, wrap?:{x, y, w, h, name?}}
detach {id}
set_override {instance, path?, kind:set|slot|replace, set?, node?, content?:[]}
reset_override {instance, path?, fields?:[], all?}
set_args {instance, args:[{name, value}]}
swap_instance {instance, of, path?}
declare_prop {component, name, def}
remove_prop {component, name}
set_slot {frame, suggested?:[], remove?, deleteContent?}
create_variable {name, variable}
update_variable {name, value?, group?, description?, unset?:[]}
rename_variable {from, to}
delete_variable {name, detach?}
set_theme_pin {node, axis, value?, inherit?}
theme_axis {action:create|rename|delete|add_value|move_value|rename_value|remove_value, axis, to?, value?, values?:[], index?, force?}
page {action:add|rename|move|delete, id?, name?, index?, key?}
Examples: kimo_read_docs path=ops.
